'' T60, RUN: a module that is not main constructs its globals, runs its 'constructor' sub
'' and then its top-level code on windows-x86_64, as fbc-modern does on Windows (Linux runs the
'' top-level code first, there and in fbc alike: .init_array walks the other way). tiko had
'' the top-level code last in the unit's list, so each platform ran the pair reversed.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/ctor-order/main.bas tests/codegen/src/ctor-order/other.bas -o tests/codegen/ctororder.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/ctororder.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: other: global constructed
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: other: constructor sub
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: other: top-level code
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: main
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: other: destructor sub
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: other: global destroyed
